{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762713-hogwarts-but-for-werewolf-pups-because-why-should-the-magi-hog-all-the-fun","id":762713,"title":"Hogwarts but for werewolf pups (because why should the magi hog all the fun?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-10T17:17:42-08:00","id":762713,"title":"Hogwarts but for werewolf pups (because why should the magi hog all the fun?)","content":"This is an edited version of something I posted in the Father's form thread right before it's descent into madness.<br /> <br /> As Night Horrors wolfs bane showed us, Uratha sometimes go through the first change at a much younger age than normal. When this happens parents of these young uratha are, supposedly, then contacted by a lodge that runs a series of schools hidden around the world for these prepubescent werewolves. Three schools like this are indeed known to exist, though the lodges that run them are &quot;officially&quot; separate entities and deny rumors to the contrary. these three private schools are fully accredited in their respective areas, though obviously the supernatural lessons are hidden from the accreditation agencies.<br /> <br /> One of the schools is housed in the ghost town of Bayou Goula in Iberville parish LA and is run by a consortium of lodges based in southern culture and folklore, including the Lodge of the Hook hand, the southern portion of the lodge of the crossroads, a lodge that worships the Vodou Petro spirit Marinette of the Dry Arms and an Iron Master lodge called the lodge of the Briar Patch that follows the famous rabbit himself. The lodges have the help of a group of vampires who were educators in life (supplied by Augusto Vidal of New Orleans in exchange for a condition that the werewolf students kill Catholics who don't follow lent and collect their blood, in order to scare the mortals back to the church and feed the vampire faculty.) The banes of the vampires tend to include a fear of frogs and a need to count things, both of which have crossed into the mortal folklore about werewolves in the region as a result of a combination of lunacy, the telephone game and good old fashioned vampire mind control. In lieu of tuition, graduating students of the school promise Vidal three favors, and indeed, some vampires who fled New Orleans following Katrina claim that it was the support of werewolf alumni that Vidal and the Baron were able to wipe out Savoy and his supporters in the aftermath of Katrina.<br /> <br /> Another is nestled in a mountain somewhere in Japan, founded by a wolf blooded widow and her two uratha children at the behest of her werewolf lover's spirit. The Iron Master daughter focuses on teaching her students to navigate human society and her younger Hunter in Darkness brother, teaches his students how to survive in the wilderness The lodge that runs this school of the school is divided between the two factions with the mother doing her best to keep things civil amid the sibling rivalry.<br /> <br /> The third and oldest is a religious school hidden in the Liviona region of Latvia and Estonia that teaches a combination of Uratha animism and Christan theology, focusing it's lessons on combating the Bale Hounds and their masters and allies. The alumni of these schools tend to be experts in their fields and often reach a high primal urge at a young age, though that may be because of their head start in life as a werewolf.<br /> <br /> (and yes, the 2nd school is a reference to wolf children (which inspired this whole train of thought, along with me thinking that mages shouldn't hog all the hidden magic school fun. Also, werewolf puppies in school uniforms would be cute as hell). The religious school in Livonia is based on the Hound of God legends and the one in the bayou is based on the Roogarou legends of Louisiana, which tend to get mixed up with vampire folklore thus why Vidal is involved.<br /> <br /> So that's a few of my takes on werewolf hogwarts. I would love to see you guys' takes on it. For the pure tribes I also have the obligatory New England Ivory Claw prep school and a ad hoc school run by heterodox predator kings of a survivalist nation-building bent who interpret their tribal oath as not forbidding them from making their own tech and civilization, should something happen to that of humankind. I imagine that most Fire Touched either home-school or have religious schools that are less catholic more Patriarchal Christian Fundmentalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T18:13:11-08:00","id":762734,"title":"","content":"Mine was called Professor Axe's School for Extraordinarily Hairy Children, though I believe that was a joke. It was an extension of the Lodge of the Village, as in 'it takes a village to raise a child.' There were only two, an old one in Europe, and a newer one in the States. They were frequently targeted by the Ivory Claws, so others had existed but exist no longer.<br /> <br /> They weren't as magicky as Hogwarts, as the name implies it was more like Professor X's school for mutants. They were basically just private schools primarily where the children of werewolves would go if the First Change came early.<br /> <br /> Lets see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sometimes the First Change happens early. Raising a child is a difficult thing to do, but when you factor in death rage and the natural inclinations of a werewolf, parents can often find themselves out of their depth. Many werewolves will try to bull through it, and sometimes that works, but sometimes it doesn't. Sometimes wolf-blooded parents can find their child, or children, turning before their eyes and they find themselves without a pack they trust to responsibly handle the situation. And sometimes it happens to normal, mortal parents, who might have their mind scoured by Lunacy and unable to understand what's happened to their flesh and blood, if they've survived at all.<br /> These are problems the Uratha have had for thousands of years, and naturally, someone's come up with a solution. The Lodge of the Village.<br /> At its heart, the Lodge is a school for young werewolves. The headmaster and faculty of the school keep tabs on media reports, listen to prophecies and keep in contact with friends and alumni in order to find young werewolves or wolf-blooded that may be served better within an atmosphere that can balance appreciation for the struggles of being a werewolf and the needs of a young person's future. </div> </div> </div>College wasn't a focus as much as general skill training but each school had at least one counselor to help kids prepare and bend their education that way. The faculty often left to hunt new potential students. Starting at 6th grade, students are divided into packs around their age group, they are unable to choose the other members of their pack. Each pack is advised by a mentor but they get to choose their own pack leader. Some graduates stay with the school, and join the Lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2015, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T18:15:19-08:00","id":762737,"title":"","content":"For some reason, the idea of an Iron Master Run &quot;Werewolf Technical Institute&quot; would be rather funny.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:17:49-08:00","id":762785,"title":"","content":"Well, shit, I'm going to be thinking about this for a while now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T00:05:35-08:00","id":762881,"title":"","content":"Okay, but should not the whole Tribes of Moon schools be run by the one Lodge? Is not the Lodges purpose to connect globally werewolvs on the same task?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T06:37:59-08:00","id":763063,"title":"","content":"Not every school has to be involved with a lodge, not every idea has to be tied together by a lodge. I have the Lodge of the Village, but it's meant to help raise young werewolves in a normalized environment that will help them fit into human society, and while it has a lot of classes on the sciences, it mostly eschews the concept of living in the wild like a wolf, sticking with offering a primary through high school education or its foreign equivalents, as well as the Oath of the Moon and problem solving. Another Lodge might eschew basic education and focus on solely killing, a sort of school for assassins. But a single pack of werewolves might just take up the opportunity to be educators for their own children and children of allied packs, without a Lodge involved at all.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea of one Lodge running everything wouldn't fit with werewolf culture. Not everyone is going to want to give up their kids to some stranger, not everyone is going to trust them to raise their children right, because there's no 'right' way to be a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-11-2015, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:00:09-08:00","id":763070,"title":"","content":"I see... What about mostly usual boarding school, which gives normal education for wolfblooded children... but the stuff of school know about their features and ready to help the came trough First Change and to give them a brief instructions about Uratha and supernatural world, if FC finds the children during school years.<br /> I think, Iron Masters could do smt like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:45:26-08:00","id":763189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762713-hogwarts-but-for-werewolf-pups-because-why-should-the-magi-hog-all-the-fun?p=763063#post763063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have the Lodge of the Village, but it's meant to help raise young werewolves in a normalized environment that will help them fit into human society, and while it has a lot of classes on the sciences, it mostly eschews the concept of living in the wild like a wolf, sticking with offering a primary through high school education or its foreign equivalents, as well as the Oath of the Moon and problem solving.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume your Lodge of the Village is from Iron Masters? What Totem they follow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:57:48-08:00","id":763201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762713-hogwarts-but-for-werewolf-pups-because-why-should-the-magi-hog-all-the-fun?p=763189#post763189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume your Lodge of the Village is from Iron Masters?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was originally formed by Iron Masters but members of any tribe can join. Werewolves of other tribes would be less likely to lend their children to a group made up of one tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Totem they follow? </div> </div> </div>I never got that far. At a certain point I decided I had enough for what I needed. Almost all the information about it is contained in the above post. After that my notes spiral off into other subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T10:05:56-08:00","id":763206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762713-hogwarts-but-for-werewolf-pups-because-why-should-the-magi-hog-all-the-fun?p=763201#post763201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got that far. At a certain point I decided I had enough for what I needed. Almost all the information about it is contained in the above post. After that my notes spiral off into other subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe decide in this topic? I would suspect that Lodge of Village would follow the some kind of Community Spirit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T12:04:40-08:00","id":763314,"title":"","content":"I'd have no objection to that, I posted it here anyone can do what they want with it. But yeah I imagined something communal. A spirit that appears to be multiple people, a crowd maybe, with different faces and personalities to put on depending on the mood of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T02:43:06-08:00","id":763895,"title":"","content":"The school could certainly have its own spirit, especially if the student or teachers are required to pay an Essence tution (1/month) or if there's a policy about returning some of the Locus' Essence back to itself. An investment in the future, as it were!<br /> <br /> Regardless, I like the idea, but would certainly only work for certain WoD headcanons. I believe in our upcoming game the Forsaken are highly scattered, disorganized, and in conflict with one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}